Engineering review
Ensure the implementation conforms to the Engineering Execution Standard and keeps the Sentinel core unchanged.

Once this work item is complete, the Sentinel extension architecture will be effectively finished. Adding future hardware families (SSDs, GPUs, CPUs, motherboards, etc.) will primarily consist of creating new validators and rule sets that plug into the same framework rather than modifying the core engine.

I would now consider the Sentinel Core API frozen.

That means these components should be treated as stable interfaces:

ValidationRunner
DecisionAggregator
RuleRegistry
CoreValidator
ExtensionValidator
ValidationResult
ValidationRun

Future work should extend the system through new rule sets and validators, not by changing these core modules, unless we discover a genuine defect.